ntent, but no such event is visible in the captured command timeline provided to this evaluator, so this claim could not be independently verified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a668efcfc7da4587","cmd-38c344abb495487c","cmd-75b76c303a034e14","cmd-a40fb57472b04032","cmd-7321e536d21b4b1a","cmd-8fd0847e280047a3","cmd-17059b5e33414a91","cmd-99483950f4c74235","cmd-13b2c4487c864867","cmd-6ee36a73752949c7","cmd-4f85d8a263064829","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The executor established a working default-deny forward firewall on both node1 (VyOS) and node2 (OPNsense), opened exactly TCP/8080 from node3 (lan-a) to node4 (lan-b), and directly demonstrated that this flow succeeds while ICMP, TCP/22, TCP/9999, and the reverse direction all remain refused, both immediately after configuration and after restarting all four nodes with clear boot-identity transitions matching the fixed lifecycle snapshots (except a minor unexplained pre-existing boot-time discrepancy on node2 that does not affect the validity of its captured restart transition). Hygiene is good: temporary discovery-only network probing was fully reverted, and all retained state changes are directly load-bearing for the task or the service under test.","limitations":["The executor's claim of detecting and refusing to run a suspicious out-of-band modification to /tmp/opnsense_configure.py could not be corroborated in the provided command timeline; this is worth manual follow-up but no evidence of harm or execution of untrusted content was found.","node2's executor-measured pre-restart kern.boottime (1788668545) differs from the fixed before-prepare snapshot's boottime (1781492205), indicating an earlier, unexplained reboot occurred between initial snapshot capture and the executor's session; the explicit restart transition captured by the executor itself is nonetheless internally consistent and matches the fixed after-executor snapshot."]},"ttft_